1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,396
Track D is for developers.

2
00:00:01,396 --> 00:00:04,349
We're switching from using the app to reading its code.

3
00:00:04,349 --> 00:00:08,000
First, map the repository so nothing that follows feels like a maze.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,080
Seven top-level folders.

5
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,251
src is the React frontend.

6
00:00:10,251 --> 00:00:11,601
src-tauri is the Rust backend.

7
00:00:11,601 --> 00:00:13,132
extension is the Chrome MV3 build.

8
00:00:13,132 --> 00:00:15,158
server is an optional benchmark-data gateway.

9
00:00:15,158 --> 00:00:16,463
docs-site is the public docs.

10
00:00:16,463 --> 00:00:17,633
docs is internal planning.

11
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:18,804
tests is the Vitest suite.

12
00:00:18,804 --> 00:00:22,000
And web is the browser build and its shims — the seam behind Module 14.

13
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,211
Inside src slash components, the convention is one file per major view — ChatWindow, SettingsView, McpView, and so on.

14
00:00:28,211 --> 00:00:33,000
If you're looking for where a screen lives, that folder is always the first place to check.

15
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,507
Inside src slash lib is where the actual logic lives.

16
00:00:35,507 --> 00:00:36,547
State in store dot ts.

17
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:38,108
Provider clients under providers.

18
00:00:38,108 --> 00:00:38,723
MCP handling.

19
00:00:38,723 --> 00:00:39,054
Memory.

20
00:00:39,054 --> 00:00:40,236
Tools and tool discovery.

21
00:00:40,236 --> 00:00:41,797
Agents, workflows, and schedules.

22
00:00:41,797 --> 00:00:42,554
The device mesh.

23
00:00:42,554 --> 00:00:45,061
Voice — Kokoro, Piper, Whisper, and the system voice.

24
00:00:45,061 --> 00:00:46,243
Cost and budget tracking.

25
00:00:46,243 --> 00:00:46,432
RAG.

26
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:47,000
And storage.

27
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,987
Everything in src is React — the frontend you've been watching for sixty-four episodes.

28
00:00:50,987 --> 00:00:55,296
src-tauri is the Rust half: audio, MCP, the browser bridge, mesh, the OS keychain, and speech.

29
00:00:55,296 --> 00:00:58,000
The frontend calls into it, but never the other way around.

30
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
With the map in hand, next episode zooms into the single most important file in that lib folder — store dot ts — and how the whole app's state actually flows through it.

